# Trivy IaC scan — accepted risks
#
# Each entry suppresses a specific finding. Remove an entry only when the
# underlying issue has been addressed in the Terraform code.

# AVD-AZU-0047: Network security group allows inbound from the internet.
#
# Intentional: the NSG on snet-aci allows port 8081 from nsg_inbound_source
# (default "*"). This is by design for internet-accessible public deployments
# where Nexus is the pip index for external users. For private deployments set
# vnet_integrated = true and nsg_inbound_source = "<your-corporate-CIDR>" in
# terraform.tfvars — the NSG rule will then only allow your network.
AVD-AZU-0047

# AZU-0012: Storage account has no network_rules block / default action is not Deny.
#
# Trivy evaluates this statically and flags the storage account because the
# network_rules block is conditional — it is only applied when
# vnet_integrated = true AND existing_subnet_id is null (managed VNet mode).
# In that mode the block IS present with default_action = "Deny", restricting
# access to the ACI subnet only.
#
# In public mode (vnet_integrated = false) the block is intentionally absent:
# ACI uses the storage account key (a 512-bit secret) to mount the Azure Files
# share over HTTPS, which is the standard ACI pattern for public deployments.
# Adding a Deny-all rule would break the file share mount in this mode.
AZU-0012
